  Edge range: [4, 10] = [C(n,2)-m, C(n,2)] = [4, 10]
  Minimum edges = n-1 = path P₀ only (all tiles absent)
  Maximum edges = C(n,2) = complete graph K_n (all tiles present)

========================================================================
  EVEN GRAPHS IN THE TILING SPACE
========================================================================

  BASE DEGREES: [1, 2, 2, 2, 1] (endpoints have 1, interior have 2)

  EVEN GRAPH CONDITION:
  For each vertex v:
    tile_deg(v) ≡ base_deg(v) mod 2
    Interior vertices: tile_deg even
    Endpoint vertices (0 and 4): tile_deg odd

  Even graphs in tiling space: 4 / 64 = 6.2%
  Expected from cycle-space theory: 2^{C(n,2) - n + 1} / 2^{n-1}
  = 2^{m - n + 1} / 1 = 2^{2} = 4
  Wait: even graphs in K_n = 2^{C(n,2)-n+1}. In the tiling subspace (fixed HP):
  The even-graph constraint removes n-1 degrees of freedom? No...
  Independent parity constraints: n-1 = 4
  Solutions: 2^{m-(n-1)} = 2^{2} = 4
  Actual: 4  Match: True

